{"id":"G1568","lemma":"ἐκθαμβέω","transliteration":"ekthambeō","sayIt":"ekthambeō","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"be awe-struck","meaning":"ἐκ-θαμβέω, -ῶ\n(ἔκθαμβος), [in LXX: Sir.30:9 * ;]\n1. to be amazed.\n2. to amaze, terrify (Sir.30:9). Pass., to be amazed, terrified: Mrk.9:15 14:33 16:5-6.†\n(AS)","glosses":["alarmed","filled with awe","deeply troubled"],"count":4,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mrk-9","v":15,"renderings":{"bsb":"they were filled with awe","kjv":"were greatly amazed"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-14","v":33,"renderings":{"bsb":"to be deeply troubled","kjv":"to be sore amazed"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-16","v":5,"renderings":{"bsb":"they were alarmed"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-16","v":6,"renderings":{"bsb":"be alarmed","kjv":"Be"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Mark 9:15","note":"Immediately all the multitude, when they saw him, were greatly amazed, and running to him, greeted him.","source":"web"}],"related":[],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}